# Machine-readable twin of "Betrieb & Migration" in v2.0.0.md (Issue #709). The release notes and
# scripts/release-rehearsal.sh walk THIS list, in this order; a change to the steps in the notes
# changes this file in the same commit.
#
# Format:  phase | expected exit | id | kind | argument
#   expected exit: one code or a comma list; audits exit 2 when they list findings, which is information, not a failure
#   phase   pre = before the deploy (read-only), migrate = prisma migrate deploy, post = after it
#   kind    sql = psql -c on the throwaway DB, script = `pnpm tsx scripts/<arg>` in the new api image,
#           migrate = `prisma migrate deploy` as the image entrypoint runs it
# Operational steps with no exit code to prove (pg_dump, the new image location ghcr.io/getclokr,
# making the packages public) stay in the notes only.
#
# DRAFT (#856): the open v2.0.0 tickets add their steps here when they merge.
#
# Deploy: the seven migrations of #836, #835 and #842 (pg_dump first). Two of them extend the
# system role templates (leave-limit:manage, leave-plan:manage for Admin, Inhaber, Salonmanager).
migrate|0|migrate-deploy|migrate|
# Probe the grants landed: the Admin (a001), Inhaber (a004) and Salonmanager (a005) templates hold
# both new keys. A count, so it always exits 0; the expected number is 0, read it in the protocol.
post|0|template-grants-836-835|sql|select count(*) from "AccessRole" where "id" in ('00000000-0000-4000-8000-00000000a001','00000000-0000-4000-8000-00000000a004','00000000-0000-4000-8000-00000000a005') and not ('leave-limit:manage:ZUGEWIESEN' = any("permissions") and 'leave-plan:manage:ZUGEWIESEN' = any("permissions"));
# After the deploy (read-only, #848): FIXED_SCHEDULE contracts whose weeklyHours differ from the day-hour sum.
# Ids only; exits 0 whether or not rows are found.
post|0|audit-848-weekly-vs-day-hours|script|audit-848-weekly-vs-day-hours.ts
